      {
        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "9f7bf00b-fa85-5ef3-b9a0-d768c5e6c36a",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Nicholas Barnewall, Patrick Barnewall, James II and VII\n- Titles: Viscount Barnewall, Lord Trimlestown\n- Places: County Dublin, Grace Dieu Abbey\n- Organizations: Irish House of Commons\n- Events: Suppression of monasteries, Glorious Revolution\n\nFacts:\n- Grace Dieu Abbey was suppressed in 1541 and was acquired by Patrick Barnewall.\n- The title Viscount Barnewall was created on 29 June 1646 for Nicholas Barnewall.\n- Nicholas Barnewall had earlier represented County Dublin in the Irish House of Commons.\n- James II and VII was born on 14 October 1633 and became King of England and Ireland as James II and King of Scotland as James VII on 6 February 1685.\n- James II and VII was deposed in the Glorious Revolution of 1688 and died on 16 September 1701.\n- The third Viscount Barnewall, a grandson of Nicholas Barnewall, supported James II and was outlawed.\n- Patrick Barnewall belonged to a junior branch of the family of Lord Trimlestown.\n- Patrick Barnewall's descendants held the title Viscount Barnewall of Kingsland.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
        "original_id": "a1d7b7c4-020a-52be-98fe-d4d6a995aa05",
        "text": "Page: Viscount Barnewall. Sentence: It was created on 29 June 1646 for Nicholas Barnewall, who had earlier represented County Dublin in the Irish House of Commons.\nPage: Viscount Barnewall. Sentence: His grandson, the third Viscount, was a supporter of James II and outlawed.\nPage: James II of England. Sentence: James II and VII (14 October 1633 – 16 September 1701) was King of England and Ireland as James II and King of Scotland as James VII, from 6 February 1685 until he was deposed in the Glorious Revolution of 1688.\nPage: Patrick Barnewall (Solicitor General). Sentence: He belonged to a junior branch of the family of Lord Trimlestown: his own descendants held the title Viscount Barnewall of Kingsland.\nPage: Grace Dieu Abbey. Sentence: Nonetheless it was suppressed in 1541 and acquired by Patrick Barnewall.",
